  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The PoC bet",
      "items": [
        "One Cloud Hypervisor microVM per workload, directly orchestrated — no Kata, no containerd",
        "Dedicated tenancy: one user per physical host; the workload is the reference adversary",
        "Deterministic teardown: kill → unmap → crypto-erase (FR-3), no residue, no wedge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundaries",
      "items": [
        "The CLH microVM is drawn External on purpose: untrusted workloads by design (doc 08)",
        "Per-workload netns with isolated veth on brporche — no workload↔workload L2 (FR-21)",
        "Tenant visibility enforced in the console adapter: a foreign id reads as 404, never 403",
        "mock KMS is a P0 stand-in: one root-only keys.json; the real KMS is its own plane"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Live environment (2026-11-21)",
